WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:07.080
A treasury analyst sees a stablecoin pair move. Which alerts deserve a closer look?

2
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:15.980
Here we use simulated quotes. The price tells us how many units of USDT buy one unit of USDC.

3
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:26.180
At zero point nine nine nine, the gap is one tenth of one percent. Exactly half a percent is also inside the band.

4
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:36.180
At zero point nine nine three, the gap reaches seven tenths of a percent. That crosses the threshold for a review.

5
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:47.280
Now open the public testnet run. These three receipts follow a single quote from Ethereum Sepolia, through Reactive Lasna, to Base Sepolia.

6
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:58.580
Start with the origin receipt. The quote event identifies the price and the observation time. Its transaction hash and log index identify this specific event.

7
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:09.380
Next, the reactive contract checks the price and requests a callback. Following the source event lets a reviewer match the second transaction to the first.

8
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:18.880
Base Sepolia recorded this alert. Its block timestamp was two seconds after the source block. Both receipts identify the same quote.

9
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:29.880
This public run had no dollar reference packet, so the system withheld its score. We now replay the same alert with synthetic price history and dollar quotes.

10
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:39.680
With corroborating references, the prototype scores the evidence for escalation. Its output becomes the suggested action for a human reviewer.

11
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:50.880
Keep the same on-chain alert and switch the context. If both dollar references stay close to one, the model can recommend continued observation.

12
00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:02.280
Remove one required dollar quote. The evidence check returns insufficient evidence and withholds the score until a matching reference is supplied.

13
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:13.180
These demonstration contexts are synthetic. They exercise the review workflow and the learned model. A real stablecoin incident requires independent market evidence.

14
00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:21.480
The repository contains the contracts, runnable tests, frozen model weights, and the evidence used in this demonstration.

15
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:29.780
Open the project readme to reproduce the run and inspect each receipt before accepting a review decision.
